returned_finding_id	P1-required-go-artifacts-absent
returned_finding	The v10 runner resolves four required immutable paths (v10-db.grammar, v10-qa.grammar, v10-drain.grammar, v10-resource.grammar), but none exists in the task research directory at review time. Therefore the promised DB/QA/drain/resource GO chain cannot be SHA-bound or independently reviewed. The existing static test exercises only missing/placeholder input failure, not a complete valid chain.
impact	v10 is a safe non-executing placeholder, not a sealed executable candidate eligible for resource creation or a gate GO.
required_correction	Create the four readonly authority artifacts with strict schemas and chain bindings, then add a valid-chain test proving the exact SHA-bound files are accepted while every stale/mismatched field fails before any child call.

returned_finding_id_2	P2-resource-registry-not-exhaustive-or-enforced
returned_finding_2	The v10 resource registry contains only known_databases C-H. It lacks runIds, container names/full IDs, and anonymous volume IDs for A-H/v4; its stated scope is not data. Further, the v10 runner neither resolves nor hashes nor validates this registry, and neither the candidate authority nor manifest binds its SHA.
impact_2	No executable control proves a future target is distinct from all retained A-H/v4 identities. This fails the required resource isolation guarantee despite the v7 import removal.
required_correction_2	Replace the registry with a readonly reconciled inventory of every prohibited A-H/v4 runId, container name/full ID, database, and anonymous volume ID. Bind the registry SHA in candidate authority, manifest, all DB/QA/drain reviews, and resource authority; machine-check all target identities against it before evidence or command issuance.
status_after_review	NO-GO-for-resource-create-or-execute; no-legacy-v7-import-is-insufficient-without-complete-enforced-authority-and-resource-chain
